1860's only post-36631 receipts sit in [37232, 39631] and [42032, 44431] (step 07); the latter is >5,000 units downstream \u2014 far beyond a 600-unit chain of the remaining length. The reachable frontier from 1006 collapses to single-successor chains (1036\u21921428 only, 1643\u2192358 only), leaving no branching that could carry the signal onto 1860's in-neighbours in time.\n\n**Confounders ruled out.** The window is busy (4,054 events, 1,765 active nodes, repeat ratio 0.01 \u2014 step 01) and the intermediaries are active around the critical moment (18 events in [36032, 37831], step 16), so a \"nothing was happening\" explanation is excluded; likewise a static path does exist at 4 hops (step 04). Neither converts into a time-respecting chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_86ef778a\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 1532, 1036, 1643, 153],\n  \"window\": [27631, 46831],\n  \"confidence\": 0.63,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 emits a single outgoing event (to 1532) around t\u224836.0-36.6k. 1532 relays only to 1036 and 1643 in the next 600-unit bucket, and those chains terminate at 1428 and 358, neither of which contacts 1860. 1860 is only ever contacted by 153, 743 and 1390, none of which lie within two hops of 1006. A static 4-hop path via the hub 153 exists when time is ignored, and the window is heavily active, but no 600-unit-gap-respecting sequence links 1006's single emission to 1860's later receipts (the nearest is in [37232,39631], the next >5k units away). Conclusion: no genuine temporal cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 48153, "total_output_tokens": 8946, "total_tokens": 57099, "total_latency_ms": 120337, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}